Multi-TD decode II (2026-08-28, evening). Submission envelope SOLVED via
LD_PRELOAD ioctl spy (/tmp/ane-spy.c, snapshot tools/) on the WORKING
libane concat run:
- tsk=0x574, td_count=2, td_size=0x274
- handles nonzero at slots {0, 4, 5, 6} (cmd, dst, src0, src1) - NOT the
  anecc tile slots {0,1,2,6,7,8} the .anec header lists; slot 1 (krn) is
  left 0 for the KMD to fill
- btsp_handle = separate BO holding payload[:td_size] (stab header + first
  0x24c bytes of TD_0), first word nid-patched (bits 16-23 = 0x40)
- pad = 0x81 (qid 1)
With that envelope, a faithful raw replica of concat EXECUTES: device
writes 3.0s into dst, no timeout. The envelope is proven; the earlier raw
attempts failed on handle slots (anec-tile slots instead of libane slots),
pad, and btsp content.

GEMM chaining status with the proven envelope:
- 2 gemm TDs at payload 0x28/0x328 (concat spacing), per-TD kernel bases
